.TH THERMALERT 1 "August 2026" "Thermalert 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
thermalert \- monitor hardware temperatures from the system status area
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B thermalert
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Thermalert
is a graphical hardware-temperature monitor designed for the GNOME desktop,
particularly Ubuntu GNOME. It reads available temperature sensors through
libsensors and displays the selected primary temperature in the desktop system
status area. It may also work in compatible desktop environments that support
GTK 3, GSettings, and AppIndicator status icons.
.PP
The indicator menu provides current sensor readings, a real-time temperature
graph, configurable warning and critical thresholds, and desktop
notifications. Notifications are enabled by default and are sent only when the
selected primary temperature enters the critical state. They can be disabled
without stopping monitoring or visual state updates. Thermalert defines no
application-specific command-line options; GTK may accept its standard options.
.PP
Automatic sensor selection prefers CPU-wide readings such as Intel Package id
0, followed by AMD Tctl, AMD Tdie, firmware CPU sensors, and individual CPU
cores. If none are present, it uses the hottest valid reading. A specific
detected sensor can be selected in Preferences. The default warning and
critical thresholds are 80 and 100 degrees Celsius, with 5 degrees of
hysteresis.
.PP
Preferences also provide an option to start Thermalert automatically when the
user logs in and an option to enable or disable critical-temperature desktop
notifications. Preference changes take effect immediately. Installing the
package does not enable autostart.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas/com.thermalert.Thermalert.gschema.xml
GSettings schema containing Thermalert preferences and defaults.
.TP
.I /usr/share/thermalert/autostart/com.thermalert.Thermalert-autostart.desktop
Reference desktop-entry template installed by the package.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart/com.thermalert.Thermalert-autostart.desktop
Per-user autostart entry created and removed by the Preferences checkbox.
If
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset, the default location is
.IR ~/.config/autostart/ .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sensors (1)
